TOP — LIVE CPU, TASK AND INTERRUPT VIEWER

Usage: top [seconds]    (default 1, range 1..60)
Keys: q quit (restores terminal).
Sources: /proc/tasks, /proc/uptime, /proc/ticks,
         /proc/context_switches, /proc/interrupts.
CPU: Idle, Busy (Console, Task, Net), per-task CPU%.
IRQ: cumulative SysTick, PendSV, SVC and UART1 counts.
IRQ/s: events per second over the last refresh interval;
       first update shows waiting (no previous sample).
DISPATCH: per-task scheduler selections, including idle.
CPU percentages use approximate 1ms tick sampling.
Uses one of six task slots. Needs ANSI terminal >= 80 columns.
MCP: use persistent PTY terminal_send/terminal_read.
